{"name":"Iris","hex":"#5a4fcf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Iris","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A taxonomic genus within the family Iridaceae – irises.","A taxonomic genus within the family Tarachodidae – certain of the mantises."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A messenger of the gods, and goddess of rainbows.","A female given name from Ancient Greek; a flower name used since the end of the 19th century."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Iris"}],"entries":[{"title":"Iris (anatomy)","blocks":[{"text":"The iris is a thin, ring-shaped structure in the eye in most mammals and birds that is responsible for controlling the diameter and size of the pupil, and thus the amount of light reaching the retina. In optical terms, the pupil is the eye's aperture, while the iris is the diaphragm. Eye color is defined by the iris."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Human_eye_close_up%2C_anterior_view.jpg/330px-Human_eye_close_up%2C_anterior_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(anatomy)","wikidata":"Q178748"},{"title":"Iris (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is an ambiguous color term, usually referring to shades ranging from blue-violet to violet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg/330px-Unidentified_Iris_Chanticleer_Purple_2868px.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(color)","wikidata":"Q6070109"},{"title":"Iris (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is a flowering plant genus of 320 accepted species with showy flowers. As well as being the scientific name, iris is also widely used as a common name for all Iris species, as well as some belonging to other closely related genera. A common name for some species is flags, while the plants of the subgenus Scorpiris are widely known as junos, particularly in horticulture. It is a popular garden flower."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(plant)","wikidata":"Q156901"},{"title":"Iris (Japanese group)","blocks":[{"text":"Iris is a Japanese idol girl group, formed in 2012 by Avex and 81 Produce. The group currently consists of five members: Saki Yamakita, Yū Serizawa, Himika Akaneya, Yuki Wakai, and Miyu Kubota. The leader is Saki Yamakita. In addition to their music career, all members are also active as voice actresses, most notably in the video game and anime series PriPara. The group has also performed themes for the anime series Wise Man's Grandchild, Magical Girl Site, Magical Sempai, and Twin Star Exorcists."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iris_(Japanese_group)","wikidata":"Q11224956"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg/500px-Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg/1280px-Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg/500px-Pupillary_light_reflex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The iris (brown coloured portion of the eye) controls the size of the pupil by contracting the sphincter pupillae and dilator pupillae muscles.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APupillary_light_reflex.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Iris_regions.jpg/500px-Iris_regions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Iris_regions.jpg/1280px-Iris_regions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Iris_regions.jpg/500px-Iris_regions.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIris_regions.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Auge_Iris.jpg/500px-Auge_Iris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Auge_Iris.jpg/1280px-Auge_Iris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Auge_Iris.jpg/500px-Auge_Iris.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Light micrograph of the iris near to the pupil. M. sph. sphincter muscle, L lens","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAuge_Iris.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Doppler_holography_of_Olivier_Martinache%27s_myosis.gif/500px-Doppler_holography_of_Olivier_Martinache%27s_myosis.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Doppler_holography_of_Olivier_Martinache%27s_myosis.gif/500px-Doppler_holography_of_Olivier_Martinache%27s_myosis.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Constriction of the pupil (miosis) observed by laser Doppler imaging reveals radial vessels of the iris.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADoppler_holography_of_Olivier_Martinache's_myosis.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Voluntary_pupil_dilation.g